{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nWith no `file_impact`, currency falls back to invalidating on ANY code-SHA change — a fail-safe measured to over-trigger: 307 of 1,457 full re-reviews (21%) ran on byte-identical material, 171 from base-SHA drift alone (b902-18af-14ed-4da1). Allowing drift without re-review, and requiring file_impact universally, are both rejected; this scopes the fail-safe instead, EXTENDING ADR-0002's per-path `{path: sha256}` machinery rather than adding a parallel trigger.\n\n## (a) Record the read-set inside the signed material\n\n**Source.** `usage_log.run_shape` emits `distinct_fetches`: `{\"tool\",\"target\"}` records where `fetch_target` returns the `path` arg for `read_file`/`list_directory` and the query STRING for `search_files`.\n\n**Normalization.** New module `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/read_set.py` reduces `distinct_fetches` to the signed read-set, in order:\n\n1. **Tool filter** — keep ONLY `tool == \"read_file\"`. `search_files` targets are query strings; `list_directory` targets are directories `_hash_file` cannot hash — dropped, not expanded (expansion would import unread files).\n2. **Root resolution** — resolve a relative target against the hash root `_hash_basis(repo_root)` (the pinned-SHA snapshot when attested, else the checkout); an absolute target is used as-is.\n3. **Containment** — `os.path.realpath`, then DROP anything not under that root (discards `../` escapes and outside-repo absolutes).\n4. **Repo-relative POSIX form** — `os.path.relpath` + `PurePath.as_posix()`, stripping a leading `./` and collapsing `.`/`..`.\n5. **Existence filter** — DROP anything not an existing regular file. A mistyped read contributed no content, so baking `_ABSENT_HASH` would let an unrelated later file creation invalidate — the over-invalidation being removed.\n6. **Dedupe + sort** — `./src/x.py` and `src/x.py` collapse to one; the manifest stays reproducible.\n\n**Plumbing.** `distinct_fetches` does not reach signing today: `sizing.usage_record` keeps only criteria/requests/token fields, and `_attach_plan_review_metrics` (`workflow/plan_review_recovery.py`) reads only `requests`. Three additive edits: `usage_record` passes it through; `pass1.aggregate_usage` unions the per-call lists (dedup on `(tool,target)`); `_attach_plan_review_metrics` unions every LLM step's, normalizes, and writes `coverage[\"read_set\"]` + `read_set_recorded`.\n\n`read_set_recorded` is set ONLY when at least one fetch was OBSERVED and survived normalization. An empty observation is deliberately NOT read as \"the review verifiably read nothing\": a runner reporting no fetch telemetry is indistinguishable from one that opened no files, and the stronger reading would scope fail-OPEN. No surviving fetch ⇒ (b) is not applied.\n\n**Signed record.** `build_manifest` gains sorted `read-path: <path>` lines plus a `read-set: <count>` marker, emitted only when recorded. The signature binds the whole manifest, so a modified read-set fails verification → `verdict=\"unsigned\"` → invalidate.\n\n## (b) Feed the read-set into the ADR-0002 dependency set\n\nScoping applies ONLY where ADR 0002 leaves a hole — all three must hold: the pre-existing set (declared `file_impact` ∪ cited paths ∪ inherited child impact) is EMPTY; the container poison rule is NOT in effect; a read-set was recorded. Then `dependency_hashes` composes **read-set ∪ expanded blast-radius entries** with the SAME machinery. The re-hash loop's STRUCTURE is unchanged — it still iterates exactly the entries recorded at signing — but each entry now DISPATCHES (below).\n\nBoth preconditions are load-bearing. Adding the blast radius to an ALREADY-scoped set would only widen it and re-create the false positive this ticket removes (an unrelated `rebar.toml` commit would invalidate a container scoped to its child's files). And a poisoned container — a live child with undeclared impact — is deliberately fail-CLOSED at whole-HEAD, since any partial scope is fail-OPEN for that undeclared impact, and read-set scoping is such a partial scope.\n\n**Blast-radius entries:** `.rebar/criteria_routing.json`, `rebar.toml`, `src/rebar/llm/criteria/**`, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json`, `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/*.md`, `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/*.yaml`. (`criteria/**` is deliberate: it holds the threshold resolver and overlay-merge core, which change outcomes with no rubric edit.)\n\nBecause the check iterates concrete recorded entries, each glob is handled two ways at ATTESTATION time:\n\n- **Expansion** — sorted `glob.glob(root_dir=base, recursive=True)`, regular files only; each match becomes an **ordinary** `dep <sha256> <path>` line, so content drift names the exact file.\n- **Membership digest** — the glob PATTERN itself is recorded as a dep entry whose digest is sha256 of its sorted, newline-joined match list, closing the addition/deletion blind spot: a rubric added after signing has no baked per-file hash but moves the digest; a deleted member moves both it and (via `_ABSENT_HASH`) its own entry.\n\nBoth sides route through ONE helper, `read_set.hash_dep_entry(entry, base=...)`, dispatching on a glob metacharacter (`*`, `?`, `[`): glob → membership digest, plain path → the existing `_hash_file` (so pre-81ca manifests re-hash byte-identically). THREE call sites convert, not two: `dependency_hashes`, `attest._rehash`, and the INLINE `_hash_file(p, base=base)` in `compute_validity`'s DEFAULT loop — distinct from `_rehash`. Missing the third would hash a glob PATTERN as a literal filename to `_ABSENT_HASH`, mismatching the signed digest and invalidating on every claim.\n\n**Fail-safes** (each falls back to invalidate-on-any-change — empty dep set → whole-HEAD): no recorded read-set (pre-change attestation, no agentic pass, no observed fetch); verification failure, including a tampered read-set; a raise during basis resolution or glob expansion, which `dependency_hashes` catches and logs.\n\n## (c) Report the basis\n\n`build_manifest` records one authenticated `currency-basis: file_impact | read-set | fail-safe` line chosen at sign time. `plan_review_status` (no LLM / no network) reads it off the signed manifest into its returned dict; a legacy manifest without it derives `file_impact` when dep lines exist, else `fail-safe`. The `--status` text renderer prints it; JSON carries the same key. ADR 0002 gains an addendum recording the read-set field, the preconditions, the composition rule, and the membership digest.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The signed manifest records the normalized read paths when fetches were observed, is absent otherwise, and a modified read-set cannot survive verification. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_drift.py -k \"read_set\" -x -q` — pinning the field, the normalization cases (non-`read_file` dropped, `./` collapsed, outside-repo and nonexistent dropped, deduped), and the tamper case.\n- [ ] With an otherwise-empty set and a moved SHA, currency reuses the ADR-0002 content-hash check over read-set ∪ blast radius: an untouched set stays current, a touched path invalidates, a file ADDED under a glob invalidates via the membership digest, and an already-scoped or poisoned set never gains the blast radius. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_drift.py -k \"no_file_impact or blast_radius or already_scoped or poisoned\" -x -q`.\n- [ ] Unverifiable read-set, pre-change attestations lacking the field, and expansion failure each fall back to invalidate-on-any-change. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_drift.py -k \"fallback\" -x -q`.\n- [ ] `rebar review-plan <id> --status` reports the basis (file_impact | read-set | fail-safe) in text and JSON. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_drift.py -k \"currency_basis\" -x -q`.\n- [ ] ADR 0002 documents the read-set field, the composition rule, and the membership digest. Verify: `grep -n \"read-set\" docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786499996247547001,"uuid":"5766cf38-bffb-4645-99fa-3b61568d1d38"}